        "problem": "Let $a=2i-3j+5k$ and $b=-i+4j+3k.$ Determine $a\\times b.$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 4)i-(2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =(-9-20)i-(6-(-5))j+(8-3)k \\\\  & =-29i-11j+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
